\title{fastglmm: Fast (Generalized) Linear Mixed Models via the 'glmm' Rust Kernel}
\description{
Fits linear models, generalized linear models, and (generalized) linear mixed models with a compiled Rust backend (the 'glmm' crate): linear mixed models by REML or maximum likelihood, and Laplace or adaptive Gauss-Hermite quadrature for binomial, Poisson, negative-binomial, and Gamma mixed models, using 'lme4'-style formulas. Estimates are validated against 'lme4', 'glmmTMB', and 'MixedModels.jl'. Deliberately scoped to fast fitting - fixed effects, Wald standard errors, variance components, conditional modes with their conditional variances, predictions on new data, simulated responses, pairwise comparisons of factor levels, and tests of fixed terms and of two nested models (anova(), compare()), with an exact restricted likelihood-ratio test for one random intercept (Crainiceanu and Ruppert (2004) \doi{10.1111/j.1467-9868.2004.00438.x}); anything the backend cannot compute honestly (profiling) is a documented error, never a silently different answer.
